From 571380b3d4724a37a639dc96f2a9a16782f33d94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:59:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: restore the pack slot after each home swap trial

borg_think_home_buy_swap_weapon() and borg_think_home_buy_swap_armour()
try each home item in the pack slot of the swap the Borg already carries
(or in the first empty slot when it carries none). After each trial they
only set that slot's quantity to zero. When the slot held the current
swap, the Borg's inventory record then lost that swap for the rest of the
store turn: step 7B evaluated armour backups as if the backup weapon were
gone, and the last notice of each step saw no swap in the pack.

With a backup weapon that resists nether in the pack and the amulet
'Evenstar' (also resists nether) in the home, the Borg therefore credited
the amulet with the high-resist bonus its backup weapon already covers,
took it from the home, stored it again on the next turn and took it back
on the turn after, leaving with a redundant amulet in its pack.

Restore the slot from safe_items after each trial, as the other home
trial loops do. An empty slot is restored to empty, as before.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#31.
---
 src/borg/borg-store-buy.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c b/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
index e6841a92f..453efe209 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
@@ -1017,8 +1017,8 @@ bool borg_think_home_buy_swap_weapon(void)
             p = weapon_swap_value;
         }
 
-        /* Restore hole */
-        borg_items[hole].iqty = 0;
+        /* Restore hole (the current swap, if the trial used its slot) */
+        memcpy(&borg_items[hole], &safe_items[hole], sizeof(borg_item));
 
         /* Restore shop item */
         memcpy(&borg_shops[BORG_HOME].ware[n], &borg_safe_shops[BORG_HOME].ware[n],
@@ -1126,8 +1126,8 @@ bool borg_think_home_buy_swap_armour(void)
         /* Evaluate the new equipment */
         p = armour_swap_value;
 
-        /* Restore hole */
-        borg_items[hole].iqty = 0;
+        /* Restore hole (the current swap, if the trial used its slot) */
+        memcpy(&borg_items[hole], &safe_items[hole], sizeof(borg_item));
 
         /* Restore shop item */
         memcpy(&borg_shops[BORG_HOME].ware[n],
